{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1506240-the-devoted-companion-kickstarter-pdf-is-out","id":1506240,"title":"The Devoted Companion Kickstarter PDF is Out.","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Deviant: The Renegades"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-03-23T10:12:08-07:00","id":1506240,"title":"The Devoted Companion Kickstarter PDF is Out.","content":"THose of you who have got it, check it out.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-23T10:17:28-07:00","id":1506242,"title":"","content":"Hey! <i>I</i> was going to post that! [mock pout]<br /> <br /> On a more serious note: I have perused it, and I like what I see. It's heavy on advice and light on crunch; but that's because that vast majority of the necessary crunch is in the core book. <br /> <br /> Hopefully, this also means that the <i>other</i> companion book won't be much longer; their development cycles were tracking with each other more or less all the way through.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-23T10:33:33-07:00","id":1506243,"title":"","content":"I agree with <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar421_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"421\" data-vbnamecard=\"421\">Dataweaver</a>. I think the content is really useful to help ST's figure out how to get into the headspace of running a Devoted campaign. I do wish they would have added more forms, variations, and etc., but I'm assuming they are saving the bulk of that stuff for the clade companion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10394-lladas","name":"lladas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10394_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-23T10:48:59-07:00","id":1506245,"title":"","content":"Pretty much. The difficulty in adding Forms, Variations, and Scars to the Devoted Companion is that there's so much overlap between Devoted and Renegades in terms of what they can do.<br /> <br /> As is, the Form we're given (an updated version of the Supersoldier Form from <b>Dark Eras 2</b>) includes the statement \u201conly the most loyal (or the most compliant) candidates receive those kind of reshaping. The last thing a conspiracy wants is a laser-focused killing machine going rogue and turning on them.\u201d<br /> <br /> The Variation we're given, Absorb Instability, is justified as being here because conspiracies love to use one Remade to keep the others in stable condition; you only need to cycle through one Remade's position, not everyone's.<br /> <br /> And the Scars, Philia and Trusting, do seem to be the sort that might lead a Remade to tend to be more corporative.<br /> <br /> You then get three Mental Merits (Library, Loose Cannon, and Moral Compass) and three Social Merits (The Company Line, Linchpin, and Staff).<br /> <br /> The bulk of the crunch in the book is about how to run Conspiracies when the players are <i>in </i>them rather than working <i>against</i> them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 03-27-2023, 01:32 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-23T10:58:39-07:00","id":1506247,"title":"","content":"That tracks-the Clade Companion is loaded with playable gimmicks by contrast, and it's more important to get the idea of what life for Deviants in conspiracies is like probably more important to grok than giving them tools to stand out.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-23T15:36:43-07:00","id":1506272,"title":"","content":"Now that this is out, I kinda want to make the Ordo Veritas from Esoterrorists as a constructive Deviant conspiracy (they're a worldwide secret society dedicated to fighting the titular esoterrorists - various cabals of occultists who have made contact with a hellish alternate dimension called the Outer Dark and spread terror and chaos to make summoning them easier, in the belief the Outer Dark will make them stereotypical magic-slinging superpowered wizards - with repeated notes that the Outer Dark's kind of occultism involves torture, human sacrifice, and diabolism, so there's no such thing as an esoterrorist who can be legitimately described as an eso-freedom fighter, at best they really don't care that the glorious arcane revolution involves things called Torture Dogs).<br /> <br /> They're perfect for an Agents game - they don't trust you, and they don't like they're working with you, but given the kind of shit they deal with - can you blame them?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-23T21:03:40-07:00","id":1506288,"title":"","content":"Outside the excellent advice for playing loyalists to a cause across a spectrum, the new Variations &amp; Scars, and the expanded conspiracy systems, is this the first time an Onyx Path book has referenced No Nut November? That may be the biggest surprise of all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1423-espritdecalmar","name":"espritdecalmar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1423_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-23T23:42:37-07:00","id":1506292,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>espritdecalmar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1506240-the-devoted-companion-kickstarter-pdf-is-out?p=1506288#post1506288\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Outside the excellent advice for playing loyalists to a cause across a spectrum, the new Variations &amp; Scars, and the expanded conspiracy systems, is this the first time an Onyx Path book has referenced No Nut November? That may be the biggest surprise of all.</div> </div> </div> </div>It is, though I admit this is the first time I've ever heard of it as some kind of alpha-male development thing. Usually, I hear about it from....men and women not particularly bothered with being alpha-male.<br /> <br /> Moving away from that topic, I continue to love how the Conspiracy system continues to be a very good and fun system for demonstrating the action of large systems and organizations, and while distracted from Renegades' particular use for it, the way it's useful for everything from occult matrices in Descent to inter-court conflict in Lost to Caucus operations in Awakening to global scale wars against the Contagion is just kind of fantastic.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-24T06:53:02-07:00","id":1506304,"title":"","content":"Is this book only something that will help with playing loyalists or do you all believe it would be valuable for a DM who is running a regular Renegade campaign? I fell in love with Deviant, but I'm just not much for the conspiracies thus far.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27618-shadowcatx","name":"ShadowcatX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27618_2.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-24T11:50:38-07:00","id":1506330,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ShadowcatX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1506240-the-devoted-companion-kickstarter-pdf-is-out?p=1506304#post1506304\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is this book only something that will help with playing loyalists or do you all believe it would be valuable for a DM who is running a regular Renegade campaign? I fell in love with Deviant, but I'm just not much for the conspiracies thus far.</div> </div> </div> </div>I confess I find a wee bit odd to like Deviant but not Conspiracies, but otherwise the answer remains yes. Everything that makes the Devoted more appealing to play also makes them more dynamic opponents and antagonists in a wide variety of context, and likewise the stuff on conspiracies is useful for building conflicts, both in terms of additional small scale beneifts for individual encounters, and providing direction for fighting large scale antagonists and maintaining a sense of shape and progress while doing so. THe brief bit for the storytelling genre and feel is also useful for nailing down precisely what sort of game you're playing, and some of the Devoted specific tools there can still be used to further nail the sort of Chronicle your Renegades want to play with a little creative reinterpretation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-24T12:58:29-07:00","id":1506339,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1506240-the-devoted-companion-kickstarter-pdf-is-out#post1506240\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">THose of you who have got it, check it out.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh! Thanks for the heads up.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>espritdecalmar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1506240-the-devoted-companion-kickstarter-pdf-is-out?p=1506288#post1506288\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Outside the excellent advice for playing loyalists to a cause across a spectrum, the new Variations &amp; Scars, and the expanded conspiracy systems</div> </div> </div> </div> Those sound promising!<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>espritdecalmar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1506240-the-devoted-companion-kickstarter-pdf-is-out?p=1506288#post1506288\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">is this the first time an Onyx Path book has referenced No Nut November? That may be the biggest surprise of all.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1506240-the-devoted-companion-kickstarter-pdf-is-out?p=1506292#post1506292\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It is, though I admit this is the first time I've ever heard of it as some kind of alpha-male development thing. Usually, I hear about it from....men and women not particularly bothered with being alpha-male.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u2026..what?\u2026.Is it at least joking like the Genius 2e book was about the necessity of killing Santa Claus and cooties being deadly?<br /> \u2026humanity is really really weird sometimes.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1506240-the-devoted-companion-kickstarter-pdf-is-out?p=1506292#post1506292\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Moving away from that topic, I continue to love how the Conspiracy system continues to be a very good and fun system for demonstrating the action of large systems and organizations, and while distracted from Renegades' particular use for it, the way it's useful for everything from occult matrices in Descent to inter-court conflict in Lost to Caucus operations in Awakening to global scale wars against the Contagion is just kind of fantastic.</div> </div> </div> </div>I definitely need to remember to use it, it is quite useful for loads of stuff besides Conspiracies. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-24T18:35:58-07:00","id":1506393,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TempleBuilder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1506240-the-devoted-companion-kickstarter-pdf-is-out?p=1506339#post1506339\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u2026..what?\u2026.Is it at least joking like the Genius 2e book was about the necessity of killing Santa Claus and cooties being deadly?<br /> \u2026humanity is really really weird sometimes.</div> </div> </div> </div>Second of four third-person omniscient blurbs of example Devoted. This particular charismatic Invasive specimen had some resentment issues in which he blamed his inability to succeed on his inability to build muscle or grow facial hair, tried the month-long abstention in the belief that the buildup of hormones would attract women, and then installed an injector he learned about on an InfoWars-style late-night radio show that he likes because it says what he's feeling.<br /> <br /> The user of the YFU-9000 Virility Self-Implant is not a good or pleasant individual!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-24T18:55:42-07:00","id":1506395,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1506240-the-devoted-companion-kickstarter-pdf-is-out?p=1506393#post1506393\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Second of four third-person omniscient blurbs of example Devoted. This particular charismatic Invasive specimen had some resentment issues in which he blamed his inability to succeed on his inability to build muscle or grow facial hair, tried the month-long abstention in the belief that the buildup of hormones would attract women, and then installed an injector he learned about on an InfoWars-style late-night radio show that he likes because it says what he's feeling.<br /> <br /> The user of the YFU-9000 Virility Self-Implant is not a good or pleasant individual!</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I broke out giggling when I saw that - because of course there's going to be some people who are slightly less pathetic than Homelander who desperately want superpowers - no matter what it does to them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-23T20:50:46-07:00","id":1509438,"title":"","content":"So the final download is out, which feels like as good a time and place as any to revisit <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1435968-crossover-cults-and-stats-if-and-how#post1436840\">the place of conspiracies compared to cults and krewes vis-a-vis advancement mechanics</a>.<br /> <br /> Player-aligned conspiracies in a Devoted-focused chronicle don't get freebie Nodes and Attributes, using only the base traits for their Standing, and must increase their traits using Effort as antagonist conspiracies do, though they can increase in Standing without cannibalizing higher-powered conspiracies by expanding their resources to meet the minimums for the next level up (as can antagonist conspiracies, which do account for extra Deviants in the cohort in Renegade-focused chronicles).<br /> <br /> Player characters can also earn Conspiracy Beats to convert to Effort like Krewe and Cult Experiences by earning Beats in pursuit of Objectives, as well as generating extra Effort by completing those Objectives; given that Devoted treat performing services for Loyalty Touchstones the same as Renegades treat pursuing their Conviction Touchstones (i.e. they earn a drip feed of Beats and Willpower scene-by-scene), this is not difficult to accomplish; Objectives add further mechanical effect to Principles on this front, as the Conspiracy Conditions Devoted player characters allow them to choose Objectives, but if the characters aren't serving as Linchpins then their Objectives <i>must</i> align with the conspiracy's Principles <i>and</i> relate to the Node they're assigned to (and even being a Linchpin only allows you to change the &quot;and&quot; to &quot;or&quot; in those criteria if you're not instead aligning it with its Virtue or Vice). Notably, Conspiracy Beats are earned one at a time at the end of a scene instead of at the end of a chapter by the number of Doctrines/Principles adhered to, putting them more in line with krewes than cults in terms of sources of expansion.<br /> <br /> Conspiracy actions still function as a source of Effort, which helps mitigate the fact that Attributes are Effort-intensive to raise (as is making new Nodes from scratch), as does the fact that conspiracy actions can still generate Effort for player-aligned conspiracies and you only need two additional Attributes and Nodes per level of Standing and new Icons only take a substantial amount of Effort if you're already over your limit \u2014 a level of Standing is functionally worth 27-45 Effort, depending on on where it gets the extra Nodes and whether it spends any extra Effort on prying them loose from someone else (the player characters being able to sabotage rival conspiracies in play without costing Effort or conspiracy actions). Exceptional successes on surveillance rolls and failure to defend conspiracy's resources when called upon can cost the conspiracy some of its conspiracy actions, and using conspiracy actions to generate Effort means you can't use them for the other benefits they can provide, but they remain capable of advancement through largely passive channels, unlike krewes and cults.<br /> <br /> Since Effort is the means by which conspiracies increase all of their traits, it's probably also worth noting that conspiracy actions also lack the stipulation that krewe actions and cult actions have where an action will always succeed (the rolls being to determine the cost in complications by the shortfall in Effort), but also lack Task Limits (since they don't roll to generate Effort) and are usable per chapter instead of per story \u2014 the main other distinction is that conspiracy actions aren't open-ended enough that you can wholesale replace the Power/Finesse + Standing roll with a character's dicepool if a Linchpin lends their face to the action.<br /> <br /> Finally, it's probably worth noting that the other balancing point is that Effort is the <i>only</i> means by which conspiracies advance themselves \u2014 cults and krewes can spend normal Experiences in addition to their respective special Experiences on traits that aren't Dominance/Esotery, but conspiracies rely on their plans going unimpeded and their Devoted advancing their Objectives to extend their influence and can't pay &quot;out of pocket&quot; to make the group stronger within its weight class.<br /> <br /> It's still an interesting contrast to the other two models, to be sure.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Extremely belated addendum that in addition to having a smaller base number of boxes to Congregation and Fidelity, Association also relies entirely on Projects (and special effects from Icons) to heal damage, whereas cults and krewes just heal over time as long as they don't take more damage, just like characters. The effect is similar \u2014 a conspiracy loses the conspiracy actions it would defer for Effort if its holdings are being attacked, and Renegades bring them down by preventing them from taking time to recover the same way rival cults and krewes hound each other to the end, except the former doesn't have the refuge of non-narrative time to work with.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":111,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","user":"Satchel","date":".  Healing addendum. 05-05-2023, 10:18 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-23T21:10:32-07:00","id":1509440,"title":"","content":"So: is this \u201cprotagonist organizations v3.0\u201d, or is it \u201cDeviant Conspiracies\u201d? That is, are the differences from cults and krewes a refinement of the previously published models in ways that address shortcomings those models have, or are the differences reflective of the specific themes of Deviant? Put another way, would it be awkward to use these rules to run cults or krewes?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-29T20:53:11-07:00","id":1510153,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1506240-the-devoted-companion-kickstarter-pdf-is-out?p=1509440#post1509440\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So: is this \u201cprotagonist organizations v3.0\u201d, or is it \u201cDeviant Conspiracies\u201d? That is, are the differences from cults and krewes a refinement of the previously published models in ways that address shortcomings those models have, or are the differences reflective of the specific themes of Deviant? Put another way, would it be awkward to use these rules to run cults or krewes?</div> </div> </div> </div>It would be pretty awkward to use these for cults and krewes, if only because conspiracies are specifically built to be made up of Baselines and Deviants and integrated into the Web of Pain and otherwise possessed of resources that don't map directly \u2014 conspiracy Icons and krewe Regalia are not remotely the same things, for instance, and the entire Privilege system wouldn't make a lick of sense to apply to something as personal-scale as a krewe or a broad-scope as a cult, but Nodes and the connections between them as a thing for deviants to either ruin on their quest for vengeance or develop as part of a basebuilding project in the name of their Principles works great.<br /> <br /> I brought it up in <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1506683-must-be-this-tall-to-be-a-world-power-reconciling-organizational-power-stats?p=1506825#post1506825\">Arc's thread on the comparison</a>, but krewes and cults both intrinsically (or near-intrinsically) have elements of their makeup with reach that conspiracies need rather high Standing to match without an Icon to open up the routes to messing with other modes of reality, and there's value in the other two having upper limits on how big of a swing their actions can make at a time without disastrous consequences being expected, especially when organizations whose default presentation isn't player-supporting directly encourage using their respective organizational actions as force multipliers led by PCs or other major assets.<br /> <br /> The presentation of an extensive list of types of conspiracy action is valuable as examples one might use for the other games, and the necessity of having at least three Nodes to create a new conspiracy can map very loosely to the fact that krewes start with a Safe Place and Scorpion Cults definitionally serve a mummy with a Tomb, but generalizing the conspiracy system to work outside of the needs of Deviant would, I think, require the game to have a more definite grasp on how groups interact with time and space and society to bridge the existing organizational mechanics with the minigame implied by the way Social Merits work way back when the GMCRU was freshly revealed and make &quot;an updated version of the organizational mechanics&quot; rather than &quot;a version of the organizational mechanics that serves the needs of Deviant as a tool for antagonists and deviants working with them, now with a more detailed toolkit.&quot;<br /> <br /> Like, being able to keep track of an organization's holdings is useful, especially in games where institutional corruption and infiltration are important concepts a la Vampire or Demon, but the Web of Pain very much informs Deviant's take on the organizational systems as antagonist resources and hierarchies of targets moreso than as force multipliers on player action or ways of contextualizing what belonging to a group gets you for membership \u2014 for that we need to expand on the Status Merit and maybe discuss supernatural real estate beyond the bare essentials of &quot;does the conceptual description of the group sound like it should have it?&quot; and &quot;are we interested in having this thing with/without narrative complications?&quot;<br /> <br /> We're still not quite at the level where you can use Group Beats and the organization mechanics to basically run a territory-control board game with zoomed-in action as appropriate for any given splat and the Companion doesn't make big enough changes to call it a full step in that direction, is I guess what I'm getting at. Mapping the Conspiracy and Setting the Scene are useful narrative tools for Deviant, and using them to tell similar types of story in other gamelines is easy enough, but those tools existed before the Devoted Companion, and its most useful additions are most useful in either expanding the way organizations are used in a standard game of Deviant or flipping the focus of the mechanics in a game of Deviant where you're working for the organizations.<br /> <br /> We're not yet at the level where we have guidelines for how hard it should be for a krewe to get Allies in the FBI and what that will allow them to do, and I feel like a proper Next Iteration Of The Organization Mechanics would need to find that missing link between &quot;a conspiracy with an appropriate Node can send the cops to your door&quot; and &quot;a character with Allies (Police) can send the cops to your door if they have enough pull or burn enough bridges.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}